  "_survivors": "L1250: moved.y goes through Abs() right after, so its sign is never observed; L1256: `<` vs `<=` differ only when x*x+y*y+z*z equals 1.0000001e-6f (0x358637BE = 4398047*2^-42) exactly. With exact float squares that can't happen: 2*0x8637BE = 4*(8b+7) is not a sum of three squares, and 4398047 = 3 mod 4 rules out fewer terms. It would need a 53-bit x87 rounding of the sum landing on the constant; the 'one ulp under' case pins the boundary from below",
  "coverage_ok": {"0048B314-0048B318": "dead: still && count>2 already left at 0048B25F, and the drop path clears [ebp-0xd]"},
